{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6gb88wvb8","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"OVERRIDE: ls20 GAME_NOT_STARTED is a reset-to-first-action idle race, not dead ARC infra","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: run 23's report (warmstart11) called the ls20 GAME_NOT_STARTED failure \"RUN INFRA-DEAD, independent of agent code.\" Run 24 disproved that. Root cause: the ARC server evicts a started game from its in-memory environment cache after a short idle gap (empirically ~150-180 seconds, load dependent on shared arcprize.org). When the ewm agent's FIRST action was followed by a slow vision reflect LLM call on local qwen-coding (about 2 minutes), the NEXT action returned GAME_NOT_STARTED_ERROR even though RESET and the first action had succeeded. Proven by a per-submit timing harness: RESET at T+0.1s, four probe actions T+16-17s all NOT_FINISHED, and after the fix post-ORIENT actions at T+65-70s all accepted. Fix (agent.py): suppress the advisory reflect LLM call during the initial probe batch via a _probing guard so probe actions fire back-to-back (T+16..17s) instead of straddling a 2-minute reflect that trips the idle eviction. A pure-idle probe up to 150s was accepted while the real 131-second reflect gap failed, bracketing the window. ARC health precheck (reset + one immediate probe) confirmed the board is live and player color 9 sits at (11,35), matching the {9,12} fix. Residual risk: the first SYNTHESIZE (not ORIENT) can still exceed the window on a cold KB; warm-start ORIENT recall (~48s) stays safely under it.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T14:22:08.000Z","vec":[-0.00496702129021287,-0.03758857399225235,0.024432647973299026,0.03087426908314228,0.08947779983282089,-0.027627427130937576,-0.0464816577732563,0.04343719035387039,0.0016489706467837095,0.06023712083697319,0.025134366005659103,-0.007479147519916296,0.00347974244505167,-0.0038654659874737263,-0.014747543260455132,0.022749163210392,0.044017642736434937,-0.0